# WN22-AC-000070: Windows Server 2022 minimum password length must be configured to 14 characters.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-ac-000070-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 minimum password length must be configured to 14 characters.`
    description `Information systems not protected with strong password schemes (including passwords of minimum length) provide the opportunity for anyone to crack the password, thus gaining access to the system and compromising the device, information, or the local network.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,account-policy,security-policy`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-53:IA-5(1)(H)`
    control_objective `WN22-AC-000070`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Password Policy >> "Minimum password length" to "14" characters.`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_IA_5_1_H `Windows Server implements IA-5(1)(H) by enforcing MinimumPasswordLength per the STIG (Minimum password length must be >= 14 characters.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `MinimumPasswordLength`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int >= 14
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
